| Purpose     | AWS               | GCP             | Azure                  |
| ----------- | ----------------- | --------------- | ---------------------- |
| Storage     | S3                | Cloud Storage   | Blob Storage           |
| Computing   | EC2               | Compute Engine  | Virtual Machines       |
| ML/AI       | SageMaker         | Vertex AI       | Azure Machine Learning |
| Serverless  | Lambda            | Cloud Functions | Azure Functions        |
| App Hosting | Elastic Beanstalk | Cloud Run       | Azure App Service      |
| Networking  | VPC               | VPC             | VNet                   |


====

Easy to remember

AWS = Amazon Cloud
GCP = Google Cloud
Azure = Microsoft Cloud

All three provide the same major cloud concepts: Storage → Computing → Hosting → Networking → AI/ML.

Azure covers the same core cloud layers as AWS, with 
Azure Machine Learning connecting Blob Storage, Virtual Machines, App Service, and VNet in one AI/ML workflow for training and deployment.

